{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"272","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Dima and Two Sequences"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Little Dima has two sequences of points with integer coordinates: sequence "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(a1, 1), (a2, 2), ..., (an, n)"},{"kind":"text","text":" and sequence "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(b1, 1), (b2, 2), ..., (bn, n)"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now Dima wants to count the number of distinct sequences of points of length "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2·n"},{"kind":"text","text":" that can be assembled from these sequences, such that the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":"-coordinates of points in the assembled sequence will "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"not decrease"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Help him with that. Note that each element of the initial sequences should be used exactly once in the assembled sequence."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Dima considers two assembled sequences "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(p1, q1), (p2, q2), ..., (p2·n, q2·n)"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x1, y1), (x2, y2), ..., (x2·n, y2·n)"},{"kind":"text","text":" distinct, if there is such "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ i ≤ 2·n)"},{"kind":"text","text":", that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(pi, qi) ≠ (xi, yi)"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"As the answer can be rather large, print the remainder from dividing the answer by number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ n ≤ 105)"},{"kind":"text","text":". The second line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a1, a2, ..., an"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ ai ≤ 109)"},{"kind":"text","text":". The third line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b1, b2, ..., bn"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ bi ≤ 109)"},{"kind":"text","text":". The numbers in the lines are separated by spaces."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The last line contains integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(2 ≤ m ≤ 109 + 7)"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the single line print the remainder after dividing the answer to the problem by number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1\n1\n2\n7\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n1 2\n2 3\n11\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample you can get only one sequence: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1, 1), (2, 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second sample you can get such sequences : "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1, 1), (2, 2), (2, 1), (3, 2)"},{"kind":"text","text":"; "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1, 1), (2, 1), (2, 2), (3, 2)"},{"kind":"text","text":". Thus, the answer is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"272D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/272/problem/D"}